## Environment: macOS

- BSD sed requires `sed -i '' 's/old/new/g' file`; BSD grep lacks `-P`. Prefer `rg`/`fd`/`sd`.
- Toolchains (Erlang/Elixir/Node, …) come from `mise`, not asdf (`~/.asdf` is gone; `.tool-versions` in each repo still drives versions; shims in `~/.local/share/mise/shims`). If `mix`/`elixir`/`node` is "command not found" in a Bash call, the session shell has a stale PATH: run `mise exec -- <cmd>` or prefix `export PATH="$HOME/.local/share/mise/shims:$PATH"`. Never suggest reinstalling asdf.
{{- else -}}
## Environment: Omarchy (Arch Linux + Hyprland)

- GNU sed: `sed -i 's/old/new/g' file` (no `''` argument). Prefer `rg`/`fd`/`sd`.
- Never run `sudo` from the Bash tool. Hand me a `! <command>` line to run myself.
- Packages via `omarchy pkg` / pacman / yay; Omarchy owns Hyprland, bar, themes, bash rc layer
